= What the experiment can detect
#image("planning-power.svg", width: 100%)
#par("At baseline3e-5 per window, doubling has99.54% modeled power. At baseline1e-6, doubling has only0.057% modeled power. These are prospective independent-arm planning assumptions; actual pair dependence may change power.")
#par("Every generator on the prime-order named curve visits the same full point set; it changes the walk order. Consecutive-bit events concern that ordering. Solinas sparsity alone does not establish ECDLP resistance or a solver advantage.")
#par("Historical deterministic outliers still exist. Random-start measurements estimate global event prevalence, not revisiting a specific known prefix. A phenomenon confined to a few starts in a2^192 or2^224 group is essentially invisible to a feasible uniform sample. Sample size follows prevalence, effect size, uncertainty and power, not a fixed field-coverage percentage.")
#par("The primary, marginal-rate and tail families are separate. Their union is nominal99.7%, subject to Welch approximation. No result excludes all alternate-bit, alternate-coordinate, higher-order or substantially rarer effects. Future work: fresh-seed replication or a separately frozen structured-start study.")
#pagebreak()
